LROSE projects use a process management layer for reliability.

LROSE docs are managed at:

  https://github.com/NCAR/lrose-docs

The realtime reliability layer is described at:

  https://github.com/NCAR/lrose-docs/blob/master/lrose-core/lrose-realtime.md

and the data management at:

  https://github.com/NCAR/lrose-docs/blob/master/lrose-core/lrose-data-flow.md

There are examples of simple projects at:

  ~/git/lrose-titan/projects

And SPOL is a good example of a more complex project:

  ~/git/spol-configuration/

For a project we use 2 main environment variables:

  $PROJ_DIR - the top level of a project hierarchy, e.g. ~/git/spol-configuration/projDir.
  $DATA_DIR - the top level of the data directory hierarchy.

System level params and scripts are located at:

  $PROJ_DIR/system/params
  $PROJ_DIR/system/scripts

Parameters and scripts are distributed, depending on role. For example:

  $PROJ_DIR/ingest/params
  $PROJ_DIR/ingest/scripts

The crontab, process mapper (procmap) and data mapper (DataMapper) files are in:

  $PROJ_DIR/control/crontab
  $PROJ_DIR/control/proc_list
  $PROJ_DIR/control/data_list

For more complex projects with multiple hosts, the host configuration is performed by a script. For example:

  ~/git/spol-configuration/projDir/system/scripts/configureHost.py

